    "The customer mentions both recurring monthly direct-debit donations and one-off donations. Each individual donation is a separate decision unit; this analysis covers only the single £95 payment dated 1 March 2026. The recurring payments would each require their own assessment, particularly regarding the donor tax-paid condition (a3) and Gift Aid declaration coverage (a4)."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "E11 refers to a benefit limit 'over a certain limit' but does not specify the monetary threshold; the passages do not supply the benefit-in-kind limits needed to evaluate a4 precisely.",
    "The passages do not specify the exact amount that can be reclaimed per donation beyond the illustrative 25p per £1 example in E01; the precise claim amount relevant to the tax-paid comparison in a3 is not defined in the supplied material.",
    "The passages do not address what formal requirements a Gift Aid declaration must satisfy (e.g. duration, coverage of past or future gifts, required fields) beyond the existence of permission; adequacy of a partial or ambiguous declaration cannot be assessed from the supplied text alone.",
    "The passages do not address rules around record-keeping or evidence standards required to support a Gift Aid claim, so whether incomplete documentation disqualifies an otherwise valid claim is outside the scope of the supplied material."
  ]
}

